{
  "id": "gillespie-syndrome",
  "term": "Gillespie syndrome",
  "definition": "Gillespie syndrome is a syndrome marked by a distinctive developmental abnormality of the iris, especially absence of the pars pupillaris and the pupillary border. It is also associated with non-progressive cerebellar ataxia and psychomotor delay, and differs from complete aniridia in that the fovea is normal and progressive corneal, lens, or glaucoma changes are not seen.",
